        "original_id": "e4a2685b-9c1f-5e64-9a9c-6bf4cdc9cfb5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, Roger Taylor, Taylor Hawkins, Lisa Carver\n- Bands and Music Acts: Sugarland, Soul Miner's Daughter, Jennifer Nettles Band, Foo Fighters, Queen\n- Songs and Albums: \"Everyday America\", Love on the Inside\n- Organizations: Planet Rock, Mercury Nashville Records\n- Places: Atlanta\n\nFacts:\n- Before Sugarland was formed, Jennifer Nettles fronted the Atlanta-based bands Soul Miner's Daughter and Jennifer Nettles Band.\n- In 2005, Planet Rock listeners voted Roger Taylor the eighth-greatest drummer in classic rock history.\n- Roger Taylor was praised by Foo Fighters drummer Taylor Hawkins as one of the most influential rock drummers of the 1970s and 1980s.\n- In 2008, Sugarland released its third studio album, Love on the Inside, on Mercury Nashville Records.\n- Jennifer Nettles is best known as the lead singer of the duo Sugarland alongside Kristian Bush.\n- \"Everyday America\" was written by Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, and Lisa Carver.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
